  "term": "esotropia",
  "definition": "Esotropia is a type of eye misalignment in which the eyes turn inward too much, creating a crossed-eye appearance. It can occur when one eye deviates inward abnormally during attempted gaze, such as with lateral rectus muscle paralysis.",
